        'Mexico',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '1857: Conquian documented in Mexico City.',
        'Late 1800s: Paco developed as gambling variant with pay-card scoring.',
        'Present: Remains popular in Mexico, especially with older players.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Paco added pay-card economics and uses five Spanish 40-card packs. Unlike Conquian, sets must be identical cards (same rank and suit), not just same rank.',
      cultural: 'Strong association with Mexican home gambling. The large deck and pay-card system are reminiscent of Panguingue.',
